values
  ('ad7ad5fc-236b-54e3-92ab-d82363af16aa', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'conic-sections'), null, 'hard',
   $q$A circle has center $(1, -3)$ and radius $4$. Which equation is the same circle written in the form $x^2 + y^2 + Dx + Ey + F = 0$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$x^2 + y^2 - x + 3y - 6 = 0$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"did-not-double-middle-term"},{"text":"$x^2 + y^2 + 2x - 6y - 6 = 0$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"flipped-center-signs"},{"text":"$x^2 + y^2 - 2x + 6y - 16 = 0$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"dropped-constants-from-expanded-squares"},{"text":"$x^2 + y^2 - 2x + 6y - 6 = 0$","is_correct":true}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$x^2 + y^2 - 2x + 6y - 6 = 0$$q$, $q$Start from $(x - 1)^2 + (y + 3)^2 = 16$. Expanding gives $x^2 - 2x + 1 + y^2 + 6y + 9 = 16$, and moving $16$ to the left gives $x^2 + y^2 - 2x + 6y - 6 = 0$ because $1 + 9 - 16 = -6$. The choice ending in $-16 = 0$ forgets the $1$ and $9$ from the expanded squares.$q$, 'draft', null)
