  ('4f5aad35-55e1-5054-b029-2f87d65ab5e5', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'conic-sections'), null, 'hard',
   $q$On a county map measured in kilometers, a cell tower at $(-6, 2)$ covers every point within $9$ km. A house is at $(0, 8)$. Is the house within range, and why?$q$, $q$[{"text":"Yes, because its squared distance $72$ is less than $81$","is_correct":true},{"text":"No, because its squared distance $136$ is greater than $81$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"flipped-center-signs"},{"text":"No, because its distance $12$ is greater than $9$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"added-legs-without-squaring"},{"text":"No, because its squared distance $72$ is greater than the radius $9$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"compared-squared-distance-to-radius"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$Yes, because its squared distance $72$ is less than $81$$q$, $q$The squared distance from the tower is $(0 - (-6))^2 + (8 - 2)^2 = 36 + 36 = 72$. The coverage circle is $(x + 6)^2 + (y - 2)^2 = 81$, and $72 < 81$, so the house is inside. Comparing $72$ with $9$ mixes a squared distance with an unsquared radius.$q$, 'draft', null)
