  ('c38f5159-d074-54f8-bd06-5daf32cb6575', null, (select id from public.skills where slug = 'conic-sections'), null, 'hard',
   $q$The point $(4, k)$ lies on the circle $(x - 1)^2 + (y - 2)^2 = 25$, and $k > 2$. What is the value of $k$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$6$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$4$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"subtracted-legs-without-squaring"},{"text":"$18$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"forgot-to-take-square-root"},{"text":"$-2$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"ignored-the-given-condition"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$6$$q$, $q$Substitute $x = 4$: $3^2 + (k - 2)^2 = 25$, so $(k - 2)^2 = 16$ and $k - 2 = 4$ or $-4$. That gives $k = 6$ or $k = -2$, and only $6$ is greater than $2$. The choice $-2$ is the other solution, which the condition $k > 2$ rules out.$q$, 'draft', null)
