   $q$The equation $x^2 + y^2 - 8x + 2y + c = 0$ is a circle with radius $5$. What is the value of $c$?$q$, $q$[{"text":"$-8$","is_correct":true},{"text":"$8$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"sign-error-moving-constant"},{"text":"$43$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"did-not-halve-linear-coefficients"},{"text":"$12$","is_correct":false,"misconception_token":"radius-not-squared"}]$q$::jsonb, $q$$-8$$q$, $q$Complete the square: $(x - 4)^2 + (y + 1)^2 = 16 + 1 - c = 17 - c$. The radius is $5$, so $17 - c = 25$ and $c = -8$. The choice $8$ comes from solving $17 + c = 25$, which forgets that $c$ changes sign when it moves across the equals sign.$q$, 'draft', null)
